TstermSymbols-Regular.ttf is a subset of JuliaMono Regular
(https://github.com/cormullion/juliamono), renamed, as its license
(OFL.txt, the SIL Open Font License 1.1) requires of modified versions,
which reserves the name JuliaMono. It holds only the symbol ranges that
Fyne's bundled DejaVu Sans Mono lacks glyphs in (see ../fonts.go), which
keeps it small. It was made from JuliaMono 0.063 with fontTools:

  pyftsubset JuliaMono-Regular.ttf \
    --unicodes=U+2000-2BFF,U+2E00-2E7F,U+1FB00-1FBFF,U+FFFD \
    --layout-features= --no-hinting --desubroutinize \
    --output-file=TstermSymbols-Regular.ttf

and then renamed, setting its name table's family to "Tsterm Symbols"
(IDs 1, 3, 4, 6, and 16), keeping the copyright notice.
